{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773449570,"nonce":"sxMEhWnE+mguwvrTOz3/leYwkQ0=","title":"settings: option to pin \"important\" issues in inbox (cannot be acknowledged away)","message":"Currently all inbox items can be acknowledged away by any agent or user action. For issues tagged \"important\", there should be a user setting in the Settings tab to keep them permanently visible in the inbox regardless of acknowledgement.\n\nBehavior:\n- When enabled (e.g. \"pin_important_inbox_items\": true), any inbox item linked to an issue with the \"important\" label is always shown in the inbox, even after ack\n- The item could appear with a distinct visual treatment (pinned, different background)\n- The user can still dismiss it, but the default ack flow does not remove it\n- Agents acknowledging inbox items should not be able to clear pinned items via the normal ack API\n\nThis pairs with the new \"important\" label convention for high-priority issues.","files":null}]}